                <pb facs="0538" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.659/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-28T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 28,
                                1919—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2978. President has approved that Doctor Charles H. Herty, now Secretary of Board
                    passing on Dye licenses, be sent to Paris as dye expert of the United
                    States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
